    <section id="outsourcing-and-tech" class="content-section">
      <h2>5. Global IT Outsourcing & Follow-the-Sun Operations</h2>
      <p>
        India's technology corridors (Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Pune, Gurgaon) drive 24/7 follow-the-sun operations for multinational corporations. Software teams utilize shift handovers:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>European Overlap Window:</strong> 1:30 PM IST – 5:30 PM IST (aligns with 9:00 AM – 1:00 PM CET).</li>
        <li><strong>US Eastern Overlap Window:</strong> 6:30 PM IST – 9:30 PM IST (aligns with 9:00 AM – 12:00 PM EDT).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For detailed scheduling frameworks, read our guide on <a href="/best-time-us-asia-meetings/">Best Time for US–Asia Business Meetings</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="dual-timezone-debate" class="content-section">
      <h2>6. The Debate Over Two Timezones in India</h2>
      <p>
        Because sunrise occurs nearly 2 hours earlier in Assam (East) than in Gujarat (West), eastern states have long advocated for a separate timezone (or the formal adoption of "Chaibagaan time" UTC+6:00). However, the Council of Scientific and Industrial Research (CSIR-NPL) maintains a unified IST policy to prevent operational confusion across Indian Railways and power grids.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Contextual Widgets Integration -->
